action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P108 on Windows: a real throw of the card and a held drag, after the app's own FREE and BOUND steps (about 10 s),
# the steps of actions/mac/P108-throw.actions. The card is 40x40 at frame x 21-61, y 130-170 DIPs (display at 125%),
# measured on the WinUI capture of 2026-10-19; it may move along x up to 300.
# THROW: 5 DIPs per move with 16 ms sleeps, let go while moving. Pass (p108-inertia.log): DRAG release velocity within
# 1 pt/s of the speed over the last 0.1 s of the points as received; coast on the closed form within 0.01 pt; end =
# release + v*0.4995 (clamped to 0...300) within 0.01 pt.
# HOLD: pressed where the throw left the card (x 117, from the DRAG predicted end), dragged 20 and held 0.3 s.
# Pass: a DRAG release 20 further on with velocity 0 and HOLD, no coast.
# Both mouseups are sent where the pointer already is (no x, y): with a position, the synthesiser's move, check and report delayed the release past the 0.1 s the velocity is measured over, and the throw read 0 pt/s.
# 2026-10-19 WinUI: pass -- release 50.40 at 51.6 pt/s (51.6 over the last 0.1 s), coast on the closed form to 76.18; HOLD released at 96.18, velocity 0, no coast.
# P108(Windows):先等 app 自己的 FREE 與 BOUND,再真正拋出卡片一次、拖曳後停住一次。通過條件見上方英文。
